# Processes and System Information

| Command | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `ps` | Show processes associated with the current session |
| `top` | Monitor running processes and system activity |
| `kill PID` | Ask a process to stop using its process ID |
| `uname -a` | Show kernel and system information |
| `df -h` | Show filesystem disk space |
| `free -h` | Show memory usage |
| `whoami` | Print the current username |
| `id` | Show user and group IDs |
